# Folia Support in GUIShop

GUIShop supports Folia (Paper's regionized multithreading fork) via FoliaLib.

## Architecture

### SchedulerUtil (`util/SchedulerUtil.java`)

Cross-platform scheduler wrapper that uses FoliaLib internally:

```java
// Initialization (in GUIShop.onEnable())
SchedulerUtil.init(this);

// Check if running on Folia
boolean isFolia = SchedulerUtil.isFolia();

// ASYNC TASKS (safe everywhere)
SchedulerUtil.runTaskAsync(() -> { /* database ops */ });
SchedulerUtil.runTaskLaterAsync(() -> { /* delayed async */ }, 20L);
SchedulerUtil.runTaskTimerAsync(() -> { /* repeating async */ }, 0L, 100L);

// ENTITY-BOUND TASKS (REQUIRED for player operations on Folia)
SchedulerUtil.runAtEntity(player, () -> { /* GUI, inventory, etc */ });
SchedulerUtil.runAtEntityLater(player, () -> { /* delayed player task */ }, 1L);
SchedulerUtil.runAtEntityTimer(player, () -> { /* repeating player task */ }, 0L, 20L);

// LOCATION-BOUND TASKS (for block/world operations)
SchedulerUtil.runAtLocation(location, () -> { /* block modification */ });

// GLOBAL TASKS (non-entity specific)
SchedulerUtil.runTask(() -> { /* global task */ });
SchedulerUtil.runTaskLater(() -> { /* delayed global */ }, 20L);

// CLEANUP
SchedulerUtil.cancelTask(wrappedTask);
SchedulerUtil.cancelAllTasks();
```

## Key Rules for Folia Compatibility

### DO NOT use direct BukkitScheduler
```java
// BAD - breaks on Folia
Bukkit.getScheduler().runTask(plugin, () -> player.updateInventory());
Bukkit.getScheduler().runTaskLater(plugin, () -> player.openInventory(inv), 1L);

// GOOD - works on Folia, Paper, and Spigot
SchedulerUtil.runAtEntity(player, () -> player.updateInventory());
SchedulerUtil.runAtEntityLater(player, () -> player.openInventory(inv), 1L);
```

### DO NOT use BukkitRunnable for player operations
```java
// BAD
new BukkitRunnable() {
    @Override public void run() {
        player.sendMessage("Hi");
    }
}.runTask(plugin);

// GOOD
SchedulerUtil.runAtEntity(player, () -> player.sendMessage("Hi"));
```

### Async is safe everywhere
```java
// Database operations - async is fine
SchedulerUtil.runTaskAsync(() -> {
    // SQLite operations
    saveToDatabase(player.getUniqueId(), data);
});
```

